## Feature #5 Increment 1 (spec §4.5) — `mixin Stream` + a source `poll_next` +
## the synchronous `for_each`/`count`/`sum` drain drivers.
##
## `mixin Stream dispatch runtime` (in `library/std/future/src/stream.rx`) is
## the async analogue of `Enumerable[T]`: one required primitive
## `def var poll_next(cx) -> Poll[Option[Int]]`, with `for_each`/`count`/`sum`
## as DEFAULT BODIES built on `poll_next` (just as `Enumerable` is defined over
## `each`). `poll_next` dispatches through the runtime vtable
## (`dispatch runtime`), so adapters can hold a heterogeneous inner stream.
##
## `for_each` is a SYNC pump driver (builds + drops a `Context`, pumps
## `poll_next`, parks on Pending, stops on `Ready(nil)` = end-of-stream) — NOT
## an `async def` and NOT `.await`-in-loop (both gated). So the v1 consumer
## driver is `stream.for_each do |x| … end` from SYNC code, not the spec
## sketch's `for x in stream` (method-level async lowering, deferred to v2).
##
## `Counter` is a finite source yielding 1, 2, 3 then `nil` (end). The pin
## drives it three ways: `for_each` (prints each), `count` (3), `sum` (6) — each
## over a FRESH Counter (the drain consumes a stream). Proves: the mixin lowers,
## `poll_next` runtime-dispatches, the sync drain drivers work, and the default
## bodies compose over `poll_next`.

class Counter
  n: Int
  limit: Int
  include Stream
  type Item = Int

  def init(limit: Int)
    self.n = 0
    self.limit = limit
  end

  def var poll_next(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Option[Int]]
    if self.n >= self.limit
      return Poll.Ready(nil)
    end
    self.n = self.n + 1
    Poll.Ready(Some(self.n))
  end
end

def main
  puts "stream start"
  var a = Counter.new(3)
  a.for_each do |v|
    puts "got #{v}"
  end
  var b = Counter.new(3)
  puts "count=#{b.count}"
  var c = Counter.new(3)
  puts "sum=#{c.sum}"
  puts "stream done"
end
